# Ordinary code has no owner: a PR needs only ci-ok. Anything that decides
# what reaches an environment, or can act as a deploy identity, needs the
# owner's approval. PR-run checks can be rewritten by the PR itself, so this
# review is the real control on the Team plan.
#
# Promotion PRs are opened by the automation App, not by the maintainer, so
# the maintainer can approve them. The maintainer's own PRs to gated paths
# merge through the admin bypass, which GitHub logs.
#
# A team should replace the owner with its own groups: devs for
# deploy/staging.json, approvers for everything else.
/deploy/staging.json        @chrisfixesit
/deploy/prod.json           @chrisfixesit
/.github/workflows/         @chrisfixesit
/.github/scripts/           @chrisfixesit
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @chrisfixesit
/scripts/delivery/          @chrisfixesit
/src/core/flags/            @chrisfixesit
/infra/                     @chrisfixesit
/infra/smoke-hook/          @chrisfixesit
/package.json               @chrisfixesit
